He brings a glass of cold water.
He places the glass on the table.
"Thank you," I say.
I take the glass.
I drink that water quickly.
Now my thirst is gone.
Now I need to go outside.
It is still very hot outside.
I take my bag and stand up.
I walk to the front counter.
That worker is at the counter.
He smiles at me.
"I need to pay," I say.
"Certainly," he says.
He looks at the computer.
